From 52b8078d19b41f886416081b78d1a23df263cd56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:54:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] SAVE never proposes the name of an existing song (#4825,
 upstream PR #4810)

BrowserFileListView::contains() only searched the window of at most 20 file items around the
current one (since #4656), so after loading "TEST 11" in a folder of 25 songs, SAVE proposed
"TEST 2" and confirming overwrote it; likewise SONG010H after SONG010. Upstream's open PR #4810,
unchanged: when the list was cut to the window, the folder is read once to find the next free
name, for numbers and letter suffixes. Numbered names now count up from the highest in the
folder (gaps aren't reused), as before #4656. Its 23 unit tests are included.

Test (beta-1.3/tests): save_name_emu.py; on 62a516c2 TEST 2 and SONG010H are overwritten.
